{"name":"Mule Fawn","hex":"#884f40","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"mule","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The generally sterile male or female hybrid offspring of a male donkey and a female horse.","The generally sterile hybrid offspring of any two species of animals."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To smuggle (illegal drugs)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mule"},{"term":"fawn","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A young deer.","A pale brown colour tinted with yellow, like that of a fawn."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of the fawn colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fawn"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mule","blocks":[{"text":"The mule is a domestic equine hybrid between a donkey and a horse. It is the offspring of a male donkey and a female horse. The horse and the donkey are different species, with different numbers of chromosomes; of the two possible first-generation hybrids between them, the mule is easier to obtain and more common than the hinny, which is the offspring of a male horse and a female donkey."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Pack_Mules_Waiting_%2815755930793%29.jpg/330px-Pack_Mules_Waiting_%2815755930793%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mule","wikidata":"Q41692"},{"title":"Deer","blocks":[{"text":"A deer or true deer is a hoofed ruminant ungulate of the family Cervidae. Cervidae is divided into subfamilies Cervinae and Capreolinae. Male deer of almost all species, as well as female reindeer, grow and shed new antlers each year. These antlers are bony extensions of the skull and are often used for combat between males."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Family_Cervidae_five_species.jpg/330px-Family_Cervidae_five_species.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deer","wikidata":"Q23390"},{"title":"Fawn (colour)","blocks":[{"text":"Fawn is a light yellowish tan colour. It is usually used in reference to clothing, soft furnishings and bedding, as well as to a dog's coat colour. It occurs in varying shades, ranging between pale tan to pale fawn to dark deer-red.\nThe first recorded use of fawn as a colour name in English was in 1789."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Oola_-_6_months.jpg/330px-Oola_-_6_months.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fawn_(colour)","wikidata":"Q2138972"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Rhyton_en_forme_de_t%C3%AAte_d%27%C3%A9quid%C3%A901.JPG/500px-Rhyton_en_forme_de_t%C3%AAte_d%27%C3%A9quid%C3%A901.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Rhyton_en_forme_de_t%C3%AAte_d%27%C3%A9quid%C3%A901.JPG/1280px-Rhyton_en_forme_de_t%C3%AAte_d%27%C3%A9quid%C3%A901.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Rhyton_en_forme_de_t%C3%AAte_d%27%C3%A9quid%C3%A901.JPG/500px-Rhyton_en_forme_de_t%C3%AAte_d%27%C3%A9quid%C3%A901.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Early fifth century BC Greek rhyton (cup) in the shape of the head of a mule, made by Brygos","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARhyton_en_forme_de_t%C3%AAte_d'%C3%A9quid%C3%A901.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Mula_et_Asinus_1578.jpg/500px-Mula_et_Asinus_1578.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Mula_et_Asinus_1578.jpg/1280px-Mula_et_Asinus_1578.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=